Package: scncall
Type: Package
Title: Single-Cell Copy-Number Calling from Long-Read Single-Cell DNA Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Luuk", "Harbers", email = "luuk.harbers@vib.be", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Calls copy-number alterations in single cells from SPLONGGET
    data (single-cell long-read DNA sequencing with 10x Multiome barcodes and
    Oxford Nanopore reads). Two channels are combined per cell and region:
    read depth (normalised against a cell-type-matched or model-based
    reference, scored against a Student-t null) and read-phased alleles
    (molecules vote for a haplotype; beta-binomial likelihood ratios of
    allelic imbalance). A normal-tissue mode calibrates its thresholds on
    self-selected null cells and reports per-cell and pooled calls; a tumour
    mode discovers clones, fits clone copy-number states and reassigns cells
    by likelihood. Inputs are the per-cell bin matrices and fragment tables
    written by the companion Python extractor 'splongcn'; outputs are flat
    tables, a result object and an export for MEDICC2 trees.
